idated":true},{"path":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438/scratchpad/money-review/money-06-account.jpg","size":211991,"isImage":true,"media_type":"image/jpeg","pathValidated":true},{"path":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438/scratchpad/money-review/money-07-billing.jpg","size":151933,"isImage":true,"media_type":"image/jpeg","pathValidated":true},{"path":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438/scratchpad/money-review/money-08-prices-hobby.jpg","size":209988,"isImage":true,"media_type":"image/jpeg","pathValidated":true},{"path":"/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438/scratchpad/money-review/money-09-sheet-states.jpg","size":88492,"isImage":true,"media_type":"image/jpeg","pathValidated":true}]},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f26e8d6b-38f3-413c-82f3-4c499cae8d1f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"11aa0607-7def-43eb-bad7-4f0ced635e7d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"output_style","style":"Plain"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fbbee382-0c14-4133-b0a3-dba95b68929f","timestamp":"2026-11-06T16:54:18.010Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nPlain output style is active. Remember to follow the specific guidelines for this style.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","hash":"456d3a683b378304b08226ba52e4ccc788e8a4e93eadbbcfc097f1afd73c9d75","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now updating the spec doc to match, then posting the boards here."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B6HKKg4JUnydodixVhcjwX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md","content":"# Money pages: which parts the app draws, which the server draws (2026-11-06)\n\nBoards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\", from y=2900 (version 121). Builder: figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_money_page.py.\n\n## Agreed by Kenneth on 2026-11-06\n\n- The server's pages open in a sheet inside the app, not in the browser.\n- The one-time purchase is called \"Credit pack\".\n- The launch offer doubles every credit amount until the end of January: a pack gives 1,000 instead of 500, Hobby 1,500 a month instead of 750, Workshop 2,000 instead of 1,000.\n\nEverything below that is not in this list is a proposal.\n\n## The rule (proposal)\n\nThe app draws credits. The server draws anything about money, inside a sheet the app owns. Where the app shows a price, it shows a sentence the server wrote and never works out a price itself.\n\n## Who draws what (proposal)\n\nApp (ships with each release):\n- **The sheet:** its frame, title, \"Open in browser\", close button, loading state and can't-load state. Never the page inside it.\n- **Welcome and Home's agent card:** the 500-credit offer and a \"See prices\" link.\n- **Composer:** ring and balance panel, credit prices on the model picker, \"About 25 credits left\", the out-of-credits card, \"+1,000 credits\" after buying.\n- **Preferences › Account:** plan name with the server-written price line, a bar per kind of credit, usage per chat (it needs the chats' local titles), the savings-alert switch. \"Get more credits\" and \"Billing\" open the sheet.\n- **Print history:** the report button and \"25 credits added\".\n\nServer (jusprinv2.obico.io), shown in the sheet:\n- **Credits and plans**, signed in or signed out.\n- **Chargebee checkout**, as today.\n- **Purchase done:** says what was added and to which account. Its \"Back to your chat\" button goes to the done address.\n- **Billing:** plan in dollars, Change plan, Cancel plan, Chargebee's portal for payment method and invoices, Delete account.\n- **Server-written lines:** the plan's price line and the savings alert.\n\n## The contract (the only part old app versions depend on; proposal)\n\n1. **GET /v2/account, as today.** The server only adds fields; the app ignores fields it doesn't know. One new field: the plan's price line, a finished sentence such as \"$16 a month with Obico Premium's 20% off\".\n2. **POST /v2/web_link {page: \"prices\" | \"billing\", from}** returns a URL that signs in once as the app's account. The sheet opens it, and \"Open in browser\" asks for a fresh one. The server answers those page names forever; a name it doesn't know opens Credits and plans. Today the app builds the pricing URL itself (`AgentConfiguration.cpp`, `cloud_pricing_url`), so this replaces that.\n3. **The done address, /v2/web/done.** When the sheet reaches it, the app closes the sheet and reads the account answer again. Checkout, a plan change and a cancel all end there. Closing with × also re-reads the account answer.\n4. **The `suggestion` slot** in the account answer (`web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py`, unused today) carries the savings alert as {text, page}. The app shows the text as written.\n\n## Constraints found\n\n- **Google sign-in can't run inside a web view.** Google blocks OAuth in embedded web views on purpose. So the signed-out sheet's buttons read \"Sign up to buy\": they close the sheet and put the person on the app's own sign-up card. Source: https://developers.googleblog.com/2021/06/upcoming-security-changes-to-googles-oauth-2.0-authorization-endpoint.html\n- **Chargebee supports its hosted checkout inside an app's web view.** It ships a React Native wrapper for exactly that. Its rule that digital goods must use in-app purchases applies to iOS and Android apps, not to a desktop app downloaded from our own site. Source: https://chargebee.com/checkout-portal-docs/react-native-wrapper-for-mobile.html\n- **Unverified:** whether a card's bank check (3-D Secure) completes inside the sheet. Test with Chargebee's test cards before building.\n- **Unverified:** browser-saved cards and password-manager extensions probably don't fill in inside the sheet. \"Open in browser\" covers that.\n\n## Open\n\n- The launch offer's edge case is my reading, not Kenneth's words: a subscription month billed on or before 31 Jan gets double.\n- The proration line on Change plan is a placeholder for Chargebee's setting.\n- Boards 5a and 5b (the old pricing page) and 4b's \"Pay as you go\" are superseded. A note on the canvas says so; their builder is unchanged.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pw4aTYEdXQpM7jv8hXrYcj","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan","input":{"done":[3],"start":4},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019V2jxH9jdRaPziWs49k3De","name":"SendUserFile","input":{"files":["/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438/scratchpad/money-review/money-00-map.jpg","/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438/scratchpad/money-review/money-01-welcome-see-prices.jpg","/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438/scratchpad/money-review/money-02-prices-signed-out.jpg","/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438/scratchpad/money-review/money-03-prices-out-of-credits.jpg","/private/tmp/claude/claude-502/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/4