{"parentUuid":"2ed1f84b-0e1e-42a7-9275-96534f970a99","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn6z4z3dr5vyoxEzXFy6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now updating the spec with the box, its contract, and the bridge leak I found."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1672,"cache_read_input_tokens":142892,"output_tokens":1075,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1672,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1075,"cache_read_input_tokens":142892,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1672},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgn6z4kfZiQKooxUXe4rR","requestRef":"9b6a1ef3-2c81-49dd-96e5-9ffc65785e2a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5b41a525-2466-4890-adbf-e0eb4aea4f6f","timestamp":"2026-11-06T17:55:06.489Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"5b41a525-2466-4890-adbf-e0eb4aea4f6f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn6z4z3dr5vyoxEzXFy6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TN4KE1imdyFbbYvfxvUmtQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin; python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md'); s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('(version 127)','(version 129)')\ns=s.replace(\"- The \\\"tell me when a plan would cost less\\\" choice\", \"- Near the top of Preferences › Account sits a box the server fills: a small page of the server's, shown in a frame, hidden when the server sends nothing. First use: the launch offer during the promotion.\\n- The \\\"tell me when a plan would cost less\\\" choice\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"5. **The `suggestion` slot**\", \"\"\"5. **The server box on Account.** The account answer carries an optional `box_url`; absent or null, the app shows nothing. Otherwise the Account page puts that URL in a sandboxed frame (scripts allowed, nothing else) and keeps it hidden until the frame's page sends `{height}` with `window.parent.postMessage`. The Account page accepts exactly two messages, and only from the server's origin: `{height}` and `{open: \"prices\" | \"billing\"}`, which opens that page in the sheet through the page link. Anything else is dropped. Those two messages are all old app versions depend on; the box's content can change any day.\n6. **The `suggestion` slot**\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"## Open\\n\", \"\"\"- **The app's native bridge reaches frames inside its pages (macOS: tested; Linux: from source).** wxWidgets adds `window.wx` to every frame, not just the page (`webview_webkit.mm`, `forMainFrameOnly:NO`; GTK uses `INJECT_ALL_FRAMES`), and hands the app the message without saying which frame sent it. A test with a plain WKWebView set up the same way: a sandboxed frame from another origin called `window.wx.postMessage` and the native handler received it. So without a fix, the server's box could send the Account page's bridge messages, such as sign out. Proposed fix, in JusPrin code only: the app gives the main page a per-load secret by running a script (which runs in the main frame only) and drops bridge messages that don't carry it. Windows (WebView2) is unchecked; its iframe messages probably arrive on a different event that wx doesn't listen to.\n- **The sheet must not carry the bridge either.** `WebView::CreateWebView` adds the bridge to every web view it makes, so the sheet that shows the server's pages needs a web view created without it.\n\n## Open\n\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"box_url\\|bridge reaches\\|version 129\" money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md | cut -c1-90; cd /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror; tail -2 README.md | cut -c1-200","description":"Add the server box and bridge finding to the spec"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1672,"cache_read_input_tokens":142892,"output_tokens":1075,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1672,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1075,"cache_read_input_tokens":142892,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1672},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TN4KE1imdyFbbYvfxvUmtQ":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin; python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md'); s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('(version 127)','(version 129)')\ns=s.replace(\"- The \\\"tell me when a plan would cost less\\\" choice\", \"- Near the top of Preferences › Account sits a box the server fills: a small page of the server's, shown in a frame, hidden when the server sends nothing. First use: the launch offer during the promotion.\\n- The \\\"tell me when a plan would cost less\\\" choice\",1)\ns=s.replace(\"5. **The `suggestion` slot**\", \"\"\"5. **The server box on Account.** The account answer carries an optional `box_url`; absent or null, the app shows nothing. Otherwise the Account page puts that URL in a sandboxed frame (scripts allowed, nothing else) and keeps it hidden until the frame's page sends `{height}` with `window.parent.postMessage`. The Account page accepts exactly two messages, and only from the server's origin: `{height}` and `{open: \"prices\" | \"billing\"}`, which opens that page in the sheet through the page link. Anything else is dropped. Those two messages are all old app versions depend on; the box's content can change any day.\n6. **The `suggestion` slot**\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"## Open\\n\", \"\"\"- **The app's native bridge reaches frames inside its pages (macOS: tested; Linux: from source).** wxWidgets adds `window.wx` to every frame, not just the page (`webview_webkit.mm`, `forMainFrameOnly:NO`; GTK uses `INJECT_ALL_FRAMES`), and hands the app the message without saying which frame sent it. A test with a plain WKWebView set up the same way: a sandboxed frame from another origin called `window.wx.postMessage` and the native handler received it. So without a fix, the server's box could send the Account page's bridge messages, such as sign out. Proposed fix, in JusPrin code only: the app gives the main page a per-load secret by running a script (which runs in the main frame only) and drops bridge messages that don't carry it. Windows (WebView2) is unchecked; its iframe messages probably arrive on a different event that wx doesn't listen to.\n- **The sheet must not carry the bridge either.** `WebView::CreateWebView` adds the bridge to every web view it makes, so the sheet that shows the server's pages needs a web view created without it.\n\n## Open\n\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"box_url\\|bridge reaches\\|version 129\" money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md | cut -c1-90; cd /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror; tail -2 README.md | cut -c1-200","description":"Add the server box and bridge finding to the spec"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgn6z4kfZiQKooxUXe4rR","requestRef":"9b6a1ef3-2c81-49dd-96e5-9ffc65785e2a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"aee523fa-e5e0-4fdb-9cd5-03a9dfc95107","timestamp":"2026-11-06T17:55:16.036Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"aee523fa-e5e0-4fdb-9cd5-03a9dfc95107","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"82d4ee8a-8593-4e1b-9496-dbce32f8f827","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TN4KE1imdyFbbYvfxvUmtQ","type":"tool_result","content":"3:Boards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\"\n46:5. **The server box on Account.** The account answer carries an optional `box_url`; abs\n56:- **The app's native bridge reaches frames inside its pages (macOS: tested; Linux: from\nSame day, version 125 (1793985486-00a4): savings-alert choice moved from Account to the Credit pack card; auto-reload on the Credit pack card and on Billing and usage; chat titles sent by the app (Ken\nSame day, version 127 (1793986042-8e50): auto-reload buys below 10 credits (Kenneth).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"8d98dae0-6564-4fd4-bd1b-d0cf0eaa0948","timestamp":"2026-11-06T17:55:16.407Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"3:Boards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\"\n46:5. **The server box on Account.** The account answer carries an optional `box_url`; abs\n56:- **The app's native bridge reaches frames inside its pages (macOS: tested; Linux: from\nSame day, version 125 (1793985486-00a4): savings-alert choice moved from Account to the Credit pack card; auto-reload on the Credit pack card and on Billing and usage; chat titles sent by the app (Ken\nSame day, version 127 (1793986042-8e50): auto-reload buys below 10 credits (Kenneth).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1,"newLines":6,"lines":[" # Money pages: which parts the app draws, which the server draws (2026-11-06)"," ","-Boards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\", from y=2900 (version 127). Builder: figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_money_page.py.","+Boards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\", from y=2900 (version 129). Builder: figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_money_page.py."," "," ## Agreed by Kenneth on 2026-11-06"," "]},{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":6,"newStart":11,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - Delete account lives at the end of Preferences › Account, not on the server's page."," - Usage per day and per chat lives on the server's page, now \"Billing and usage\", not in the app."," - The app sends each chat's title to the server with its usage, and the server keeps it beside the chat id.","+- Near the top of Preferences › Account sits a box the server fills: a small page of the server's, shown in a frame, hidden when the server sends nothing. First use: the launch offer during the promotion."," - The \"tell me when a plan would cost less\" choice sits on the Credit pack card of the pricing page, not in Preferences. Auto-reload is offered there and on Billing and usage."," "," Everything below that is not in this list is a proposal."]},{"oldStart":42,"oldLines":7,"newStart":43,"newLines":8,"lines":[" 2. **POST /v2/web_link {page: \"prices\" | \"billing\", from}** returns a URL that signs in once as the app's account. The sheet opens it, and \"Open in browser\" asks for a fresh one. The server answers those page names forever; a name it doesn't know opens Credits and plans. Today the app builds the pricing URL itself (`AgentConfiguration.cpp`, `cloud_pricing_url`), so this replaces that."," 3. **The done address, /v2/web/done.** When the sheet reaches it, the app closes the sheet and reads the account answer again. Checkout, a plan change and a cancel all end there. Closing with × also re-reads the account answer."," 4. **DELETE /v2/account** deletes the account; the app then signs out.","-5. **The `suggestion` slot** in the account answer (`web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py`, unused today) carries the savings alert as {text, page}. The app shows the text as written.","+5. **The server box on Account.** The account answer carries an optional `box_url`; absent or null, the app shows nothing. Otherwise the Account page puts that URL in a sandboxed frame (scripts allowed, nothing else) and keeps it hidden until the frame's page sends `{height}` with `window.parent.postMessage`. The Account page accepts exactly two messages, and only from the server's origin: `{height}` and `{open: \"prices\" | \"billing\"}`, which opens that page in the sheet through the page link. Anything else is dropped. Those two messages are all old app versions depend on; the box's content can change any day.","+6. **The `suggestion` slot** in the account answer (`web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py`, unused today) carries the savings alert as {text, page}. The app shows the text as written."," "," ## Constraints found"," "]},{"oldStart":51,"oldLines":6,"newStart":53,"newLines":9,"lines":[" - **Unverified:** whether a card's bank check (3-D Secure) completes inside the sheet. Test with Chargebee's test cards before building."," - **Unverified:** browser-saved cards and password-manager extensions probably don't fill in inside the sheet. \"Open in browser\" covers that."," ","+- **The app's native bridge reaches frames inside its pages (macOS: tested; Linux: from source).** wxWidgets adds `window.wx` to every frame, not just the page (`webview_webkit.mm`, `forMainFrameOnly:NO`; GTK uses `INJECT_ALL_FRAMES`), and hands the app the message without saying which frame sent it. A test with a plain WKWebView set up the same way: a sandboxed frame from another origin called `window.wx.postMessage` and the native handler received it. So without a fix, the server's box could send the Account page's bridge messages, such as sign out. Proposed fix, in JusPrin code only: the app gives the main page a per-load secret by running a script (which runs in the main frame only) and drops bridge messages that don't carry it. Windows (WebView2) is unchecked; its iframe messages probably arrive on a different event that wx doesn't listen to.","+- **The sheet must not carry the bridge either.** `WebView::CreateWebView` adds the bridge to every web view it makes, so the sheet that shows the server's pages needs a web view created without it.","+"," ## Open"," "," - The launch offer's edge case is my reading, not Kenneth's words: a subscription month billed on or before 31 Jan gets double."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md"]}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aee523fa-e5e0-4fdb-9cd5-03a9dfc95107","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
