{"type":"agent-name","agentName":"Design the no-wizard first-run flow on the canvas","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438"}
{"type":"mode","mode":"normal","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438"}
{"type":"atis-latch","atis":"805e11cb567452db","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438"}
{"type":"frame-link","artifactCount":2,"sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","timestamp":"2026-11-06T17:55:25.015Z"}
{"parentUuid":"f9c183db-aa99-449a-849f-3ec8b78d96a9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn71WffcNuGhcm2Kef5C","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've drawn the server's box near the top of Preferences › Account (it's on the canvas now, and I sent you the screenshot). Before anyone builds it, there's a security problem to fix.\n\n**How it looks.** Say Alex has no plan and opens Account in January. Under the \"Account\" heading they see a purple \"Launch celebration\" box: \"Double credits on everything\", \"Credit packs and every month of every plan, until 31 Jan\", and a \"See the offer\" button. A Workshop subscriber opens the same page and the server sends them nothing, so there's no box and no gap.\n\n**How it would work (my proposal):**\n- The account data the app already loads gets one optional field: the URL of the server's small page. If it's missing, the box stays hidden. It also stays hidden when the app is offline or using the person's own API key.\n- The app puts that page in a locked-down frame. The frame stays hidden until the server's page has loaded and reported its height, so an empty or half-loaded box never shows.\n- The frame can send the Account page only two messages, and only from our server's address:\n  - its height;\n  - \"open prices\" or \"open billing\", which opens that page in the sheet.\n- The Account page drops any other message. Those two messages are all that old app versions rely on. Everything inside the box can change any day without an app release.\n\n**The security problem.** I checked the question I flagged last time. The app's link to its native side does reach a frame inside the page.\n- On macOS, wxWidgets adds that link to every frame in the page, not just the main one. When a message comes in, it doesn't tell the app which frame sent it.\n- I tested this with a bare macOS web view set up the way wxWidgets sets one up. A sandboxed frame from another site sent a message, and the native side received it.\n- On Linux, the wxWidgets source does the same. I haven't checked Windows.\n- So as things stand, a page inside the box could send the same commands as the Account page itself, such as sign out.\n\n**The fix I propose.** It's all in JusPrin's own code; nothing in the wxWidgets dependency changes. Each time the Account page loads, the app hands it a secret. It does this by running a script, and that script only runs in the main page, never in a frame. The app then ignores any message to its native side that doesn't carry the secret.\n\nThe sheet I proposed for showing the server's pages needs similar care. The app's usual way of creating a web view always adds this link, so the sheet needs a web view created without it.\n\nAll of this, including the leak and the fix, is in `money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md` (untracked). The board is version 129 of the canvas: https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":634,"cache_read_input_tokens":146503,"output_tokens":877,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":634,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":877,"cache_read_input_tokens":146503,"cache_creation_input_tokens":634,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":634},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgn71WSWjdgVLC5JSkBxS","requestRef":"a1ef269f-ff0e-45a0-9d83-2a7cf1267b4d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid