{"parentUuid":"b2311fb9-d112-4e55-b708-fd3c4baf7c3a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn7xNgisfGEYuS5nck4V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013172z3muM1csw7FFGvNLUf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin; python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md'); s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('(version 129)','(version 130)')\no=\"- Near the top of Preferences › Account sits a box the server fills: a small page of the server's, shown in a frame, hidden when the server sends nothing. First use: the launch offer during the promotion.\\n\"\nassert o in s\ns=s.replace(o,\"- Near the top of Preferences › Account sits a box the server fills: words and pictures in a frame, hidden when the server sends nothing. It has no links or buttons. The server decides per person: signed out, \\\"sign up today\\\"; signed in but never paid, the offer; subscribed or bought a pack, nothing. First use: the launch offer during the promotion.\\n\")\na=s.index(\"5. **The server box on Account.**\"); b=s.index(\"6. **The `suggestion` slot**\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"5. **The server box on Account.** A small request, GET /v2/account_box, sent with the sign-in token when there is one, so it also answers signed-out people. It returns the box's HTML or nothing; nothing means no box. The Account page puts the HTML in a frame sandboxed with scripts off (`sandbox=\"allow-same-origin\"`, via `srcdoc`), measures its height itself, and only then shows it. With scripts off, nothing in the box can reach the app, and links can't open, so the box is words and pictures only. The HTML brings its own styles; it can't use the app's CSS. Old app versions depend only on \"HTML or nothing\".\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\no2=\"So without a fix, the server's box could send the Account page's bridge messages, such as sign out. Proposed fix, in JusPrin code only: the app gives the main page a per-load secret by running a script (which runs in the main frame only) and drops bridge messages that don't carry it.\"\nassert o2 in s\ns=s.replace(o2,\"A frame with scripts allowed could therefore send the Account page's bridge messages, such as sign out. The box above avoids this by running no scripts: tested the same way, with `sandbox=\\\"allow-same-origin\\\"` the frame's script didn't run, nothing reached the native side, and the parent page read the frame's height. Should a frame ever need scripts, the fix (proposal, JusPrin code only) is a per-load secret the app hands the main page by running a script, which runs in the main frame only; the app drops bridge messages without it.\")\np.write_text(s)\nEOF\necho 'Same day, version 130: the server box has no links or buttons (Kenneth): a scripts-off frame; Account shows it signed out (\"sign up today\"), signed in never paid (the offer), and not at all for a Workshop subscriber.' >> /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/README.md; grep -n \"account_box\\|allow-same-origin\" money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md | cut -c1-80","description":"Update the spec and log for the words-only box"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_read_input_tokens":165804,"output_tokens":1448,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":395,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1448,"cache_read_input_tokens":165804,"cache_creation_input_tokens":395,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":395},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013172z3muM1csw7FFGvNLUf":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin; python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md'); s=p.read_text()\ns=s.replace('(version 129)','(version 130)')\no=\"- Near the top of Preferences › Account sits a box the server fills: a small page of the server's, shown in a frame, hidden when the server sends nothing. First use: the launch offer during the promotion.\\n\"\nassert o in s\ns=s.replace(o,\"- Near the top of Preferences › Account sits a box the server fills: words and pictures in a frame, hidden when the server sends nothing. It has no links or buttons. The server decides per person: signed out, \\\"sign up today\\\"; signed in but never paid, the offer; subscribed or bought a pack, nothing. First use: the launch offer during the promotion.\\n\")\na=s.index(\"5. **The server box on Account.**\"); b=s.index(\"6. **The `suggestion` slot**\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"5. **The server box on Account.** A small request, GET /v2/account_box, sent with the sign-in token when there is one, so it also answers signed-out people. It returns the box's HTML or nothing; nothing means no box. The Account page puts the HTML in a frame sandboxed with scripts off (`sandbox=\"allow-same-origin\"`, via `srcdoc`), measures its height itself, and only then shows it. With scripts off, nothing in the box can reach the app, and links can't open, so the box is words and pictures only. The HTML brings its own styles; it can't use the app's CSS. Old app versions depend only on \"HTML or nothing\".\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\no2=\"So without a fix, the server's box could send the Account page's bridge messages, such as sign out. Proposed fix, in JusPrin code only: the app gives the main page a per-load secret by running a script (which runs in the main frame only) and drops bridge messages that don't carry it.\"\nassert o2 in s\ns=s.replace(o2,\"A frame with scripts allowed could therefore send the Account page's bridge messages, such as sign out. The box above avoids this by running no scripts: tested the same way, with `sandbox=\\\"allow-same-origin\\\"` the frame's script didn't run, nothing reached the native side, and the parent page read the frame's height. Should a frame ever need scripts, the fix (proposal, JusPrin code only) is a per-load secret the app hands the main page by running a script, which runs in the main frame only; the app drops bridge messages without it.\")\np.write_text(s)\nEOF\necho 'Same day, version 130: the server box has no links or buttons (Kenneth): a scripts-off frame; Account shows it signed out (\"sign up today\"), signed in never paid (the offer), and not at all for a Workshop subscriber.' >> /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/README.md; grep -n \"account_box\\|allow-same-origin\" money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md | cut -c1-80","description":"Update the spec and log for the words-only box"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgn7xNU5jh49VpnHKqxtw","requestRef":"9e246374-3dcd-488b-96e6-9d73b5c79b61","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cf6f7390-9623-4288-992f-5066389180d3","timestamp":"2026-11-06T18:08:01.207Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
