{"parentUuid":"cf6f7390-9623-4288-992f-5066389180d3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f05d84df-2f6c-48b0-9d64-cc17cb4f781a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013172z3muM1csw7FFGvNLUf","type":"tool_result","content":"46:5. **The server box on Account.** A small request, GET /v2/account_box, sent \n56:- **The app's native bridge reaches frames inside its pages (macOS: tested; L","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d57ea781-fdf9-43db-ad08-dcf52e422c9a","timestamp":"2026-11-06T18:08:01.606Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"46:5. **The server box on Account.** A small request, GET /v2/account_box, sent \n56:- **The app's native bridge reaches frames inside its pages (macOS: tested; L","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":6,"newStart":1,"newLines":6,"lines":[" # Money pages: which parts the app draws, which the server draws (2026-11-06)"," ","-Boards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\", from y=2900 (version 129). Builder: figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_money_page.py.","+Boards: canvas https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ, page \"Credits & plans\", from y=2900 (version 130). Builder: figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_money_page.py."," "," ## Agreed by Kenneth on 2026-11-06"," "]},{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":7,"newStart":11,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - Delete account lives at the end of Preferences › Account, not on the server's page."," - Usage per day and per chat lives on the server's page, now \"Billing and usage\", not in the app."," - The app sends each chat's title to the server with its usage, and the server keeps it beside the chat id.","-- Near the top of Preferences › Account sits a box the server fills: a small page of the server's, shown in a frame, hidden when the server sends nothing. First use: the launch offer during the promotion.","+- Near the top of Preferences › Account sits a box the server fills: words and pictures in a frame, hidden when the server sends nothing. It has no links or buttons. The server decides per person: signed out, \"sign up today\"; signed in but never paid, the offer; subscribed or bought a pack, nothing. First use: the launch offer during the promotion."," - The \"tell me when a plan would cost less\" choice sits on the Credit pack card of the pricing page, not in Preferences. Auto-reload is offered there and on Billing and usage."," "," Everything below that is not in this list is a proposal."]},{"oldStart":43,"oldLines":7,"newStart":43,"newLines":7,"lines":[" 2. **POST /v2/web_link {page: \"prices\" | \"billing\", from}** returns a URL that signs in once as the app's account. The sheet opens it, and \"Open in browser\" asks for a fresh one. The server answers those page names forever; a name it doesn't know opens Credits and plans. Today the app builds the pricing URL itself (`AgentConfiguration.cpp`, `cloud_pricing_url`), so this replaces that."," 3. **The done address, /v2/web/done.** When the sheet reaches it, the app closes the sheet and reads the account answer again. Checkout, a plan change and a cancel all end there. Closing with × also re-reads the account answer."," 4. **DELETE /v2/account** deletes the account; the app then signs out.","-5. **The server box on Account.** The account answer carries an optional `box_url`; absent or null, the app shows nothing. Otherwise the Account page puts that URL in a sandboxed frame (scripts allowed, nothing else) and keeps it hidden until the frame's page sends `{height}` with `window.parent.postMessage`. The Account page accepts exactly two messages, and only from the server's origin: `{height}` and `{open: \"prices\" | \"billing\"}`, which opens that page in the sheet through the page link. Anything else is dropped. Those two messages are all old app versions depend on; the box's content can change any day.","+5. **The server box on Account.** A small request, GET /v2/account_box, sent with the sign-in token when there is one, so it also answers signed-out people. It returns the box's HTML or nothing; nothing means no box. The Account page puts the HTML in a frame sandboxed with scripts off (`sandbox=\"allow-same-origin\"`, via `srcdoc`), measures its height itself, and only then shows it. With scripts off, nothing in the box can reach the app, and links can't open, so the box is words and pictures only. The HTML brings its own styles; it can't use the app's CSS. Old app versions depend only on \"HTML or nothing\"."," 6. **The `suggestion` slot** in the account answer (`web_ent/jusprin/ledger/account.py`, unused today) carries the savings alert as {text, page}. The app shows the text as written."," "," ## Constraints found"]},{"oldStart":53,"oldLines":7,"newStart":53,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - **Unverified:** whether a card's bank check (3-D Secure) completes inside the sheet. Test with Chargebee's test cards before building."," - **Unverified:** browser-saved cards and password-manager extensions probably don't fill in inside the sheet. \"Open in browser\" covers that."," ","-- **The app's native bridge reaches frames inside its pages (macOS: tested; Linux: from source).** wxWidgets adds `window.wx` to every frame, not just the page (`webview_webkit.mm`, `forMainFrameOnly:NO`; GTK uses `INJECT_ALL_FRAMES`), and hands the app the message without saying which frame sent it. A test with a plain WKWebView set up the same way: a sandboxed frame from another origin called `window.wx.postMessage` and the native handler received it. So without a fix, the server's box could send the Account page's bridge messages, such as sign out. Proposed fix, in JusPrin code only: the app gives the main page a per-load secret by running a script (which runs in the main frame only) and drops bridge messages that don't carry it. Windows (WebView2) is unchecked; its iframe messages probably arrive on a different event that wx doesn't listen to.","+- **The app's native bridge reaches frames inside its pages (macOS: tested; Linux: from source).** wxWidgets adds `window.wx` to every frame, not just the page (`webview_webkit.mm`, `forMainFrameOnly:NO`; GTK uses `INJECT_ALL_FRAMES`), and hands the app the message without saying which frame sent it. A test with a plain WKWebView set up the same way: a sandboxed frame from another origin called `window.wx.postMessage` and the native handler received it. A frame with scripts allowed could therefore send the Account page's bridge messages, such as sign out. The box above avoids this by running no scripts: tested the same way, with `sandbox=\"allow-same-origin\"` the frame's script didn't run, nothing reached the native side, and the parent page read the frame's height. Should a frame ever need scripts, the fix (proposal, JusPrin code only) is a per-load secret the app hands the main page by running a script, which runs in the main frame only; the app drops bridge messages without it. Windows (WebView2) is unchecked; its iframe messages probably arrive on a different event that wx doesn't listen to."," - **The sheet must not carry the bridge either.** `WebView::CreateWebView` adds the bridge to every web view it makes, so the sheet that shows the server's pages needs a web view created without it."," "," ## Open"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin/money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md"]}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cf6f7390-9623-4288-992f-5066389180d3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
