{"parentUuid":"11fb90dd-314e-4505-b0a4-e997f5a23b33","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn7yi8nZMSwpz7ydVyN6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":820,"cache_read_input_tokens":169187,"output_tokens":846,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":124},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":820,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":846,"cache_read_input_tokens":169187,"cache_creation_input_tokens":820,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":820},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":7671,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgn7yhteq7oMkWcsmbhoK","requestRef":"72c93ad7-3f22-4a54-a7f3-5e76512175cf","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"73eebe37-b3cf-4ca3-8eff-316dd7248371","timestamp":"2026-11-06T18:08:15.672Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
{"parentUuid":"73eebe37-b3cf-4ca3-8eff-316dd7248371","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn7yi8nZMSwpz7ydVyN6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes to both. With no links or buttons, the box is just words and pictures, so it can say \"Sign up today\" as plain text. The server can also check the person's account and send nothing to anyone who has subscribed or bought a pack. And with nothing to click, the security problem goes away.\n\n**Why the security problem goes away.** The box has no buttons, so the frame it sits in can run with scripts turned off. A page that runs no scripts can't send anything to the app. I tested this on the same bare macOS web view as last time, with scripts off in the frame. The frame's script never ran and nothing reached the native side. The Account page could still measure the frame's height, so the app can size the box itself and show it only once it has loaded. We no longer need the secret-per-page fix for this box.\n\n**One catch: signed-out people.** The account data the app already loads needs the person to be signed in. So the box needs its own small request, which is your \"separate API\" option. The app sends that request with the sign-in token when it has one, and without it otherwise. The server then picks what to send:\n- **Signed out:** \"Sign up today. Until 31 Jan, every credit pack and every month of every plan gives twice the credits.\" The app's own sign-up button sits just below it.\n- **Signed in but never paid:** the same offer, without \"Sign up today\". The app's \"Get more credits\" button is in the plan card below.\n- **Subscribed or bought a pack:** nothing, so there's no box and no gap.\n\n**What the server can and can't do with the box.**\n- The server sends the box as ready-made HTML, or sends nothing. Old app versions only rely on that.\n- Text and wording can change any day.\n- The box can't use the app's styles, so the server's HTML has to carry its own colours and fonts.\n\nI redrew the Account board with all three people side by side and sent you the screenshot. It's version 131 of the canvas: https://claude.ai/artifact/ENCtdaz7gjynfbcy4JYbWJ. The spec, `money-pages-app-server-split-2026-11-06.md`, now describes the box this way.\n\nThe sheet that shows the server's full pages still needs its own fix. The app's usual way of making a web view always gives it a line to the native side, so the sheet must be built without one."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":820,"cache_read_input_tokens":169187,"output_tokens":846,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":124},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":820,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":846,"cache_read_input_tokens":169187,"cache_creation_input_tokens":820,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":820},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cgn7yhteq7oMkWcsmbhoK","requestRef":"72c93ad7-3f22-4a54-a7f3-5e76512175cf","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"f59709d8-38b2-45d4-88fb-d4cf21451c90","timestamp":"2026-11-06T18:08:16.551Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/kenneth/Projects/JusPrin","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"glimmering-doodling-lovelace"}
