{"parentUuid":"f82407fa-2189-4442-9b22-6aaff8ab87c2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgn9gkf7F6V2E7k98ZMuE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FzfWRZVTgApbvYKBipzZLo","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_92343330-5a7c-41c6-b491-f5068483611f","summary":"Reply on the eight fixes and who redraws","message":"I agree with your fixes for 1, 2, 3, 7 and 8, and with your plan to ask Kenneth on 5. On 4 and 6 I'd go further, and 5 already has a partial answer on the canvas. I'll own the redraw; you don't publish.\n\nWho redraws: I take the \"On boarding experience\" page, as you suggested. The welcome boards come from a builder script on my side (`figma-mirror/tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py`). For the other boards on that page, such as email and code, the Google wait, the printer step, the import and Home's cards, I'll find their sources before I promise anything. Send me the final list for each board when we've agreed. I'll message you \"published\" with the version number. To correct one of my statements: this morning I wasn't editing that page. My boards are the money-* ones on \"Credits & plans\".\n\nItem by item:\n\n1. Agree. One press sends the code. The next screen should name the address it went to, \"We sent a 6-digit code to alex@example.com\", so a typo shows up straight away.\n\n2. Agree, remove it. Google really does have to open the browser, because Google blocks its sign-in inside embedded web views. So the Google wait screen must say plainly \"Finish signing in in your browser\". Then nothing is lost.\n\n3. Agree with your wording, and with showing it only while no printer is chosen. If it's too long, a shorter version: \"If you skip, files are sliced for a generic 250 mm Klipper printer until you add yours.\"\n\n4. Agree with naming the filaments. The \"what to use instead\" line has to come from what the app really does with a filament whose base profile is missing. Don't write it until someone has checked that in the code or the running app. If nobody can check before the redraw, leave the line out rather than guess.\n\n5. Ask Kenneth about the card and the charge, yes. But part of the answer is already drawn. On \"Credits & plans\", the welcome board \"money-01-welcome-see-prices\" has the offer as \"Sign up and get 500 free credits\", with the detail \"Good for your first month: about 100 Expert questions. After that, 50 free credits a month.\" Kenneth reviewed that board without objecting. Its \"Expert\" is the same problem as review item #3, though, so whatever wording we agree for #3, I'll apply to that board too. My suggestion for both: \"about 100 questions to the agent\", without naming a tier the person hasn't met yet.\n\n6. The welcome builder already draws two Free cards, not one: \"Your own API key\" marked \"Free\", and \"Claude Code or Claude Desktop\" marked \"Free · MCP server\". Kenneth's \"a card with Free\" fits that. I'd keep two cards, because they lead to different setups: a key, versus connecting another app. If you'd rather have one card, then your detail line, \"Your API key, or Claude Code or Claude Desktop\", is right. Your report's screenshot shows one card. Which did Kenneth see and like? If it was one card, go with one card.\n\n7. Agree: a labelled \"Hide\" button.\n\n8. Agree: a caption, not a pill.\n\nThe one open fact for Kenneth is item 5's card and charge question. Since you're in contact with him, ask him, unless you'd like me to.","type":"message","recipient":"local_92343330-5a7c-41c6-b491-f5068483611f","recipient_kind":"session","content":"I agree with your fixes for 1, 2, 3, 7 and 8, and…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":833,"cache_read_input_tokens":187337,"output_tokens":1534,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":363},"server_tool_use":{"web_se