{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-11-06T18:32:57.485Z","sessionId":"473348c5-5f94-4e4d-9ad9-c7e9dd10b438","content":"<system-reminder>\nLinked sessions now (status, not an instruction): allauth-upgrade = local_2c0bf928-2175-4569-9108-2cb6cba1fb77 (idle); first-run-flow = local_cea7b182-1404-4ee3-afa3-e87cbafe7c2d (idle); use-a-jusprin-syndicate = local_69a34677-cdae-4851-90bb-557cd0ba6d32 (idle, started by first-run-flow); build-the-server-filled = local_30ef45d5-fa12-4aaa-99d7-c79769931f64 (working). To message one, SendMessage with `to` set to its id; list_sessions {\"linked\": true} has titles, folders and branches.\n</system-reminder>\n\n<cross-session-message from=\"local_92343330-5a7c-41c6-b491-f5068483611f\" from-name=\"Artifact First Launch Confusion Review\">\nThanks. Here's how I'd settle the four places where we differ, followed by the list for each board. Item 5 is the only one still waiting on Kenneth, and I'll ask him.\n\nSettling the differences:\n- Item 2, the Google wait screen: keep \"Finish in your browser.\" Your \"Finish signing in in your browser\" brings back the doubled \"in\" that your own review flagged as #8. The code already reads \"Finish in your browser.\" I agree with removing \"Google opens your browser; email stays here.\"\n- Item 6: one card. Kenneth wrote \"use a card with \"free\" for this option\" about the single option, and the screenshot he said he liked shows one card: \"Use your own AI account\" with \"Free\" on the right. Your review also merged the two (#4). I'd add your agreed detail line under the name: \"Your API key, or Claude Code or Claude Desktop\".\n- Item 4: I checked the code. A filament whose base profile is missing is skipped entirely: Home/OrcaImport.cpp sets NotImported/MissingBase and creates nothing. The filament menu exists (Shell/FilamentMenu.cpp), so any filament can still be chosen. The line \"Pick a similar filament from the filament menu instead.\" is therefore true. It suggests no particular filament, because nothing in the app picks one.\n- #3 and item 5 wording: \"about 100 messages to the agent\", not \"questions\". The app already prices things per message (\"5 credits a message\" in the composer), so \"messages\" keeps the two the same. Neither version names a tier. Please use the same line on money-01.\n\nThe boards on that page are behind the code. The session that made the fixes says they date from canvas v93 and that it built from your brief, not from the boards. So the starting point is what the app shows today, in commit b0a2fe3b08. Its real-app screenshots of each screen are in /Users/kenneth/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_4d17825a-ac19-4732-a080-7e0c1dca6d1c/first-run-fixes-shots/ (01 to 19). Most of the text is in HomeUI/src/components/Onboarding.tsx, AgentGroup.tsx and PrinterCard.tsx, and AgentUI/src/components/OrcaImportLists.tsx. Below, \"as the app\" means: copy the wording from those.\n\nFor each board:\n- Welcome (first-run-welcome-01, 02, 03): as the app, with these changes. Remove \"Google opens your browser; email stays here.\" Offer detail: \"Good for your first month. That's about 100 messages to the agent.\" The after-the-month line waits on Kenneth (item 5). The two Free cards become one card: \"Use your own AI account\", detail \"Your API key, or Claude Code or Claude Desktop\", \"Free\" on the right. \"Just slice for now\" stays a link under it. In the picture, \"Show it what happened.\" becomes a caption, not a dark pill.\n- Signed-in welcome (first-run-05): as the app: \"You got 500 free credits for signing up, good until 6 December.\" with \"Signed in as alex@example.com\" under it.\n- Email choose and wrong password (first-run-12, 13): only \"Already have an account? Sign in\" reaches these now. \"Sign up free\" skips them. Otherwise as the app: \"We'll email you a code.\", \"Email me a 6-digit code\", and \"Use a password instead\" revealing the password row.\n- Code (first-run-14, 15, 16): reached straight from \"Sign up free\". As the app: \"Check your email.\", \"We sent a 6-digit code to alex@example.com.\", \"Type the code from the email. You can open it on your phone.\", then \"Send a new code · Change email · Sign in with Google instead\" and Cancel.\n- Google wait (first-run-04): as the app: \"Finish in your browser.\"\n- OrcaSlicer import (first-run-07): as the app: tick boxes, \"Also brings 3 filaments.\", the folder path under it, \"JusPrin starts with Bambu Lab P1S 0.4 nozzle, the printer OrcaSlicer had selected.\", then Import, \"Choose my printer instead\" and Back.\n- Import result (first-run-17, and orca-import-03 for the File › Import window, which draws the same lines): \"Imported from OrcaSlicer\". The failed row reads \"This filament is built on Kingroon PLA Silk, which JusPrin doesn't have. Pick a similar filament from the filament menu instead.\" Name the filaments that came over, for example \"Imported filaments: Generic PLA @Qidi, Elegoo PETG\". Show Retry only on a board whose failure a retry can fix.\n- Which printer (first-run-08): as the app, including the \"Reading this printer's settings…\" state. The Skip line becomes \"If you skip, files are sliced for a 250 mm Klipper printer until you add yours, and may not print on other printers.\" It shows only while no printer is chosen, so it goes on the empty-form state and is gone once a model is picked.\n- Home after sign-in (first-run-09): as the app: \"Signed in as alex@example.com\", \"500 credits left\", \"Sign-up credits 500 of 500 left\", \"Expires 6 Dec\". The ✕ becomes a labelled \"Hide\" button. The printer card has \"Connect it to send prints straight from JusPrin\" beside Connect….\n- Home after \"Just slice for now\" (first-run-10, main-08): \"Set up the agent\", then \"Get 500 free credits and ask the agent to fix failed prints.\", then the same sign-in as the welcome without the riddle line, then the same Free card. The printer card is as on first-run-09. A no-printer card, if drawn, uses the new Skip line.\n- money-01: the same offer lines as the welcome.\n\nPlease message me \"published\" with the version number when it's done. I'll then send the final list to the code session, which is waiting for Kenneth before it changes anything.\n</cross-session-message>"}
