{"parentUuid":"13bab8e4-82d8-4625-9316-8c6c87b73622","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnA86MU9S5TXukoPSabR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E785mHDJcvKSr3VBRcbLoM","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/kenneth/.claude/projects/-Users-kenneth-Projects-JusPrin/figma-mirror/tools/composer; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path('build_first_run_page.py'); s = p.read_text()\ndef rep(old, new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:90]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\nrep(\"'Pick how the agent thinks: sign in for 500 credits, your own API key, Claude Code or Claude Desktop, or Just slice for now.'\",\n    \"'Sign up for 500 free credits with Google or an email code, use your own AI account, or Just slice for now.'\")\nrep(\"\"\"                ('Continue with email', 'A code or the password (12, 13), then the six-digit code (14 to 16), then Signed in (05).'),\n                ('Your own API key, or Claude Code or Claude Desktop', 'Preferences › Agent opens over the welcome (06). Saving a key, or Done, closes it and goes to Your printer. Closing it unfinished goes back to the welcome.'),\"\"\",\n\"\"\"                ('Sign up free', 'The code goes out at once: typing it (14), a wrong code (15), a code that no longer works (16), then Signed in (05).'),\n                ('Already have an account? Sign in', 'A code or the password (12), a wrong password (13), then the code steps or Signed in (05).'),\n                ('Use your own AI account', 'Preferences › Agent opens over the welcome (06): an API key, or Claude Code or Claude Desktop. Saving a key, or Done, closes it and goes to Your printer. Closing it unfinished goes back to the welcome.'),\"\"\")\nrep(\"Import, then Imported (17), then Home. Start fresh shows 08.'),\",\n    \"Import, then Imported (17), then Home. Choose my printer instead shows 08.'),\\n\"\n    \"                ('A printer chosen', 'Its settings are read (18), then Continue goes to Home.'),\")\nrep(\"'Brand, model and nozzle, then Continue. Skip for now is the other way on.'\", \"'Brand, model and nozzle, then Continue. Skip for now says what skipping does.'\")\nrep(\"'The welcome (01) and what each door leads to. Signing in ends on 05, which moves on by itself after a moment. Your own API key and '\\n\"\n    \"      'Claude Code or Claude Desktop open Preferences over the welcome (06); Claude Code or Claude Desktop is the same window on Connect an AI tool. '\\n\"\n    \"      'Just slice for now goes straight to Your printer.')\",\n    \"'The welcome (01) and what each door leads to. Signing in ends on 05, which moves on by itself after a moment. Use your own AI account, '\\n\"\n    \"      'one card marked Free (Kenneth, 2026-11-06), opens Preferences over the welcome (06). Just slice for now goes straight to Your printer.\\\\n\\\\n'\\n\"\n    \"      'Redrawn 2026-11-06 to match the app on commit b0a2fe3b08, with the fixes agreed that day: no “Google opens your browser; email stays here.”, '\\n\"\n    \"      'the offer without the Expert tier, the clip’s words as a caption, and one Free card. What happens after the first month is still to be '\\n\"\n    \"      'decided by Kenneth, so no line says it yet.')\")\nrep(\"'Continue with Google opens the browser and the card waits (04). Continue with email stays in the app: a code or the password (12), '\\n\"\n    \"      'a wrong password (13), typing the code (14), a wrong code (15), a code that no longer works (16). Each ends on Signed in (05). '\\n\"\n    \"      'Built 2026-11-03 (Kenneth: “Yes, build it”), not released.')\",\n    \"'Continue with Google opens the browser and the card waits (04). Sign up free sends the code at once (agreed 2026-11-06): typing it (14), '\\n\"\n    \"      'a wrong code (15), a code that no longer works (16). Only “Already have an account? Sign in” asks for a code or the password (12), '\\n\"\n    \"      'and a wrong password shows on 13. Each ends on Signed in (05).')\")\nrep(\"'what the welcome finished, a headline that says why the app asks, brand, model and nozzle, Continue, and Skip for now with what '\\n\"\n    \"      'skipping means, and, as one quiet line, the OrcaSlicer folder choice Kenneth approved on 2026-11-03. No step counter\",\n    \"'what the welcome finished, a headline that says why the app asks, brand, model and nozzle, Continue, and Skip for now with what '\\n\"\n    \"      'skipping would do, shown only while no printer is chosen (agreed 2026-11-06). Once one is, its settings are read (18). No step counter\")\nrep(\"Import shows what it brought (17), and Start fresh shows 08.')\",\n    \"Import shows what it brought (17), and Choose my printer instead shows 08. Imported names the filaments that came over, and one that couldn’t '\\n\"\n    \"      'come over says to pick a similar one from the filament menu (agreed 2026-11-06).')\")\np.write_text(s)\nprint('ok part 3')\nPYEOF\ncd ../..; python3 tools/composer/build_first_run_page.py work-first-run-v2/project 2>&1 | tail -2; python3 tools/composer/render_dc.py work-first-run-v2 $TMPDIR/onb first-run-welcome-01-clip-beat-1.dc.html first-run-05-welcome-signed-in.dc.html first-run-04-welcome-sign-in-waiting.dc.html first-run-12-email-choose.dc.html first-run-13-email-wrong-password.dc.html first-run-14-email-code.dc.html first-run-16-email-code-spent.dc.html first-run-07-orcaslicer-import.dc.html first-run-08-add-printer.dc.html first-run-18-printer-reading.dc.html first-run-17-import-result.dc.html first-run-09-home-after-sign-in.dc.html first-run-10-home-after-just-slice.dc.html orca-import-03-imported.dc.html first-run-11-flow.dc.html 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Fix the map wording, rebuild and render the boards","timeout":500000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens