{"parentUuid":"d9c4c89d-547d-4f61-8ced-4c9ba9b087e7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7f668efa-054d-4724-a408-dee0c47b11e4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ri7tQK6RnWw3dr6G1eGmbr","type":"tool_result","content":"boards = []\nboards.append(board('money-00-map.dc.html', 'Who draws which part, and what crosses between the app and the server',\n    'The in-app sheet, Credit pack and the launch offer are Kenneth’s (2026-11-06); the rest is a proposal. The app’s parts read only the account answer; the server’s pages open only through a page link (prices, billing) and end at the done address. Those plus the server-written lines are the whole contract an old app version depends on.', money_map()))\nboards.append(patched('money-01-welcome-see-prices.dc.html', WELCOME, 'First meeting · the welcome says what the credits are and links to prices',\n    'Proposal. Only the offer card’s two lines change: the headline says the credits are free, the detail says how long they last, what 500 buys and what comes after, and “See prices” opens Credits and plans in the sheet. The rest is the welcome as drawn on On boarding experience, where the agreed wording fixes for its other lines also apply.',\n    [(f'>{escape(OFFER_OLD[0])}<', f'>{escape(OFFER_NEW[0])}<'), (f'>{escape(OFFER_OLD[1])}<', f'>{OFFER_NEW[1]}<')]))\nbuild_credits_page.py:511:def patched(filename, source, title, intro, changes):\nbuild_credits_page.py-512-    \"\"\"A live onboarding screen with only its account wording changed, so everything else stays as approved, in a captioned frame.\"\"\"\nbuild_credits_page.py-513-    s = (proj / source).read_text()\nbuild_credits_page.py-514-    for old, new in changes:\nbuild_credits_page.py-515-        assert old in s, old\nbuild_credits_page.py-516-        s = s.replace(old, new)\nbuild_credits_page.py-517-    return board(filename, title, intro, s[s.index('</helmet>') + 9:s.index('</x-dc>')].strip())\nbuild_credits_page.py-518-\nbuild_cre