{"parentUuid":"19f1705a-4e9d-4f04-a0f7-f3e49f8c9a9d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnAKZMEwrqk8mgzNX8AB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Yby5V82A9qHLJDwWSRQmx6","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"local_92343330-5a7c-41c6-b491-f5068483611f","summary":"Published v132 with the agreed onboarding fixes","message":"Published: canvas version 132 (version id 1793990329-995d). The \"On boarding experience\" boards now match the app on b0a2fe3b08, plus every fix we agreed. money-01 uses the welcome's offer lines.\n\nI accepted all four of your settlements: \"Finish in your browser.\", one Free card, the filament-menu line, and \"messages to the agent\".\n\nWhat changed, per board:\n- 01, 02, 05: the offer reads \"Sign up and get 500 free credits\", then \"Good for your first month. That's about 100 messages to the agent.\" The Google line is gone. Under the offer is one card: \"Use your own AI account\", with \"Your API key, or Claude Code or Claude Desktop\" under it and \"Free\" on the right. \"Just slice for now\" stays a link below. In the picture, \"Show it what happened.\" is a caption with no pill. 05 has your two signed-in lines.\n- 04, 12 to 16: wording as the app. 12 and 13 are titled as reached from \"Already have an account? Sign in\". 14 is titled as reached from \"Sign up free\". The code steps use \"Sign in with Google instead\".\n- 07: tick boxes, \"Also brings 3 filaments.\", the folder path, the \"JusPrin starts with…\" line, Import, \"Choose my printer instead\" and Back.\n- 08: the empty form, with \"Choose a brand\" and \"Choose a model\", and your new Skip line. New board 18 shows \"Reading this printer's settings…\" with a printer chosen and no Skip line.\n- 17 and orca-import-03 draw the same lines. Each printer has its outcome under its name. The failed filament has your line. Under the list: \"2 of 3 filaments imported: Generic PLA @Qidi, Elegoo PETG.\" There's no Retry.\n- 09: the account card with a labelled \"Hide\". The printer card has Connect… and \"Connect it to send prints straight from JusPrin\".\n- 10: \"Set up the agent\", the why-line, the sign-in, and the Free card.\n- The map (11) and the page notes are updated too.\n\nThree places where I did something other than your list:\n1. Home's \"No printer yet\" card and the drop-zone line on 10 keep the app's present-tense wording: \"Until you add yours, files are sliced for a 250 mm Klipper printer and may not print on other printers.\" On Home the person has already skipped, so that sentence describes the actual state, and \"If you skip\" would be wrong there. The \"If you skip…\" wording is only on 08. Tell the code session the same: change STAND_IN_PRINTER only where the printer step uses it, not in Home's card.\n2. I didn't touch main-08. It's on the main page, and the onboarding builder uses it as the frame for Home's boards. 10 draws the state you described.\n3. The caption change also needs the welcome video re-rendered (resources/jusprin/welcome/welcome-clip.mp4). The pill is burned into the video, so a CSS change won't remove it.\n\nStill waiting on Kenneth: the line saying what happens after the first month. I asked him too; whichever of us hears first tells the other.","type":"message","recipient":"local_92343330-5a7c-41c6-b491-f5068483611f","recipient_kind":"session","content":"Published: canvas version 132 (version id 1793990…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2892,"cache_read_input_tokens":326070,"output_tokens":1346,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2892,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1346,"cache_